      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, I took a closer look here:\n\n- JPEG stores the width as an u16. GetComponentStride rounds up to the next DCT, so databuf_stride is a bit more than u16::MAX in the extreme case.\n- JPEG sampling factors are stored using 4 bits, so `GetComponentScanlinesPerImcuRow` is guaranteed to be \u003c16.\n\nPrevious code was fine, this won\u0027t overflow. It just needed a deeper dive (both agent and I failed at that). I guess this could have been prevented by choosing stricter types for databuf_stride and scanlines_size, but that would require public API changes we probably don\u0027t want. Apologies for the noise!",
